# Signing keys, without exception. There is deliberately no negation here: this
# repository is public, and the debug keystore is not a throwaway — it is the key
# every published build has been signed with, so anyone holding it could sign an
# APK that Android accepts as an update to an existing install. Its password being
# the well-known "android" does not make the key pair inside it any less unique.
*.keystore
*.jks

# Symlink to the local agentic workspace. Machine-specific and not part of the project.
.aw

# Release artefacts: the APK handed to a GitHub release, built fresh each time.
/dist/
